			<div class="content" id="post-content-1807944">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Review&nbsp;enclosed</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Thank&nbsp;you!&nbsp;Please&nbsp;come&nbsp;again!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I think &quot;as this cause SCP-1940&quot; should be &quot;as this causes SCP-1940&quot; or &quot;as this will cause SCP-1940&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If the room in question is too small to fit these, its inner contents will appear to shrink to smaller proportions. However, this only affects SCP-1940-1, the counter and cash register, and the various shelves and displays holding products: the previous contents of the room do not change in size.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>First things first, I think you want a semicolon, not a colon. Secondly, I'd probably refer to &quot;If the room in question is too small to fit these <strong>items</strong>&quot; but that may be personal taste.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Instances of SCP-1940-1 are of either gender</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I have no idea where the Foundation is on the gender debate, but if you want to play it safe, that could be &quot;any gender&quot; to indicate that they might be trans/herm/neuter/etc</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1940-1 can be killed, causing another instance of SCP-1940-1 to materialize when not under observation, and will try to reason with its attacker.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;and will&quot; should probably be &quot;which will&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An instance of SCP-1940 will cease to exist after all products of SCP-1940 are purchased.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Suggest &quot;products within SCP-1940&quot; or maybe &quot;products offered for sale within SCP-1940&quot; to indicate that they are the items that were reclassified by the SCP rather than ones created by it? Next sentence, again, you probably want a semicolon.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Attempts of surveillance to observe how SCP-1940 develops has been met with failure, due to all surveillance equipment being taken as products in SCP-1940. Recorded data show SCP-1940-1 locating any equipment and shutting then off before converting them into SCP-1940-2, though it will deny doing so upon interview.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;has been met&quot; should be &quot;have met&quot;. &quot;shutting then off&quot; should be &quot;shutting <strong>them</strong> off&quot;</p>
<p>I agree with the prior commentary on your thread that storing used condoms is very bizarre behavior. If you want to imply Agent Blackbox has been up to some infidelity, maybe change it to &quot;used panties&quot; or, more blatantly, &quot;used underwear belonging to his mistress or wife&quot;?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, you have a few typos, but I like it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
